  %% Algorithm: the reversible point-add construction
  Phases["Affine P plus Q in eight in-place phases: x -= Qx, y -= Qy, y /= x gives lambda, x += 3Qx, x -= lambda squared, y *= x, y -= Qy, x = Qx - x"]
  Coord["Coordinate blocks: classical-offset subtract, add 3Qx, final subtract and reverse subtract with windowed modular folds"]
  Square["Low-space modular square: x -= lambda squared"]
  DivLeg["Division leg: y /= x by the forward GCD Skywalk walk, 415 steps"]
  MulLeg["Multiplication leg: y *= x by the reversed walk, 415 steps"]
  Walk["GCD Skywalk walk: Stein binary GCD on signed rails holding u+v and u; parity routes the even rail to halving, one controlled rail exchange and one signed add per step, no magnitude compare"]
  Tape["History tape: orientation and sign-flip bits take 3 joint values; 5 steps packed in 8 wires inside the freed rail top bits"]
  Cells["Payload cells: Sigma and Delta frame, Sigma to Sigma -/+ Delta over 2 mod p then swap on sign flip; chunked adds with windowed carries, flags and folds"]
  Cleanup["Cleanup: payloads coincide at the division endpoint and one is cleared with CNOTs; reversing the walk consumes the tape and restores the denominator; every phase returns scratch to zero"]
  Post["Exact post-passes: redundant CCX removal on product, affine, quadratic and truth supports, measurement absorption; inherited 96-gate X identity tail"]

